From: Akshay Kakatkar <me@kakatkarakshay.dev>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: select valid link for MLO multicast offload

mac80211 leaves the MLO link field at zero for hardware-encapsulated
802.3 frames because the field is not used for those frames. For multicast
offload, the TX path also has no STA, so ath12k_mac_get_tx_link() treats
zero as an explicit link ID and returns it unchanged.

When an AP MLD does not contain link zero, ath12k consequently fails to
resolve ahvif->link[0] and drops the frame before multicast replication.

For a hardware-encapsulated frame without a STA, select the first
driver-backed valid link when zero is not valid. This initial link only
provides a valid arvif; the multicast path still replicates the frame using
each link's own arvif. If no driver-backed valid link remains, retain the
existing behavior and drop the frame.

Fixes: 648a121bafa3 ("wifi: ath12k: ath12k_mac_op_tx(): MLO support")
Signed-off-by: Akshay Kakatkar <me@kakatkarakshay.dev>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wifi7/hw.c
@@ -921,7 +921,14 @@ static void ath12k_wifi7_mac_op_tx(struc
 	}
 
 	/* handle only for MLO case, use deflink for non MLO case */
 	if (ieee80211_vif_is_mld(vif)) {
+		links_map = vif->valid_links & ahvif->links_map;
+		if (!sta &&
+		    (info_flags & IEEE80211_TX_CTL_HW_80211_ENCAP) &&
+		    link_id == ATH12K_DEFAULT_LINK_ID &&
+		    !(vif->valid_links & BIT(link_id)) && links_map)
+			link_id = __ffs(links_map);
+
 		link_id = ath12k_mac_get_tx_link(sta, vif, link_id, skb, info_flags);
 		if (link_id >= IEEE80211_MLD_MAX_NUM_LINKS) {
 			ieee80211_free_txskb(hw, skb);
